-- title:
--   Coefficients of the generic level-ℓ modular polynomial lie in ℚ[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime, let $\zeta$ be a unit of the cyclotomic field `CyclotomicField ℓ ℚ` whose underlying element is a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, and let $c : \mathbb{N} \to$ `LaurentSeries ℚ` be a family of rational Laurent series. Assume `PhiGenDescends ℓ ζ c`: for every $k$, the $k$-th coefficient of the monic polynomial $\prod_{i : \mathrm{Fin}(\ell+1)} (X - C(\mathrm{conj}\ \ell\ \zeta\ i))$ over the Laurent series of the cyclotomic field, whose roots are the formal conjugates `conj ℓ ζ i` obtained by applying the substitution `cosetSubst ζ (cosetA ℓ i) (cosetB ℓ i)` to the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of the formal $q$-expansion `jq`, equals the coefficientwise image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ ℓ (c k)`, the series $c_k$ with its exponents multiplied by $\ell$. Then, for every natural number $k$, the series $c_k$ lies in `Algebra.adjoin ℚ {jq}`, the $\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra of `LaurentSeries ℚ` generated by `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot$`ofPowerSeries jNumQ`. Thus each solution of the descent equations is a polynomial in $j$ with rational coefficients.
--
--   This is the analytic leg of the construction of the modular polynomial $\Phi_\ell$: it identifies the coefficients of $\prod_i (X - j\circ\beta_i)$, taken over the $\ell+1$ Hecke cosets of level $\ell$, as elements of $\mathbb{Q}[j]$, so that $\Phi_\ell(X,Y) \in \mathbb{Q}[X,Y]$ with $\Phi_\ell(X,j) = \prod_i (X - j\circ\beta_i)$. It is used in the construction of the modular polynomial data for $X_0(\ell)$ and in the statements about splitting and about the weighted support of that data; integrality, symmetry and the degree bounds are established separately.
